---
/* THE ICON SPRITE — rendered once, at the top of <body>, by Base.astro.

   One inline sprite rather than 30 separate files or 30 inline <svg> blocks:
   - one request (zero, actually — it ships in the HTML),
   - every icon inherits `currentColor`, so the same glyph works on the cream page and on the
     near-black bands without a second copy,
   - a page that uses six icons costs six 40-byte <use> refs, not six full paths.

   DRAWING RULES, so the set stays one family:
   - 24x24 viewBox, geometry on whole or half pixels wherever possible.
   - Stroke only. No fills — `fill="none"` is set on the parent <svg> in Icon.astro.
   - stroke-width 1.6, round caps and joins. This matches the terminal's own nav icons (1.8 at
     18px) once scaled down, so the site and the product read as one system.
   - Hard-cornered where the design language is hard-cornered (boxes, grids, bars) and curved only
     where the subject genuinely is (globe, coins, crescent). The house rule bans rounded corners
     on UI chrome, not on drawings of round things.

   `aria-hidden` lives on the <svg> in Icon.astro — every icon here is decorative and sits beside
   a real text label, so none of them should be announced.
*/
